            <ArticleTitle>A new way to assess pain in laboring women: replacing the rating scale with a &quot;coping&quot; algorithm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>404-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1751-486X.2008.00364.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 2001, the Joint Commission introduced a compliance guideline designed to improve pain care for all patients. In response, most hospitals created a pain policy that was intended to be implemented for all hospital patients. This article describes how nurses in a busy labor and delivery unit created a pain management policy that met the Joint Commission's goals and also supported their desire to assist laboring women in the most appropriate way possible.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
